  <prompt>
    Add/extend unit tests for the field-mapping rule DTO projection (mappingType/expression/defaultValue/
    isRequired/compatibilityMode), measure BFF publish size delta, run a CVE scan, and prove the existing
    UpdateRelatedButton push path still deserializes correctly after the additive DTO change.
  </prompt>

  <role>SPAARKE platform developer. Expert in xUnit + the Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests conventions (ADR-038 integration-heavy pyramid).</role>

  <goal>Tests cover the new rule-DTO fields; the push path is proven unaffected; publish size + CVE status are reported in task notes.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>§10 BFF Hygiene requires test update + publish-size verification for every BFF-touching task. The push endpoint (PushFieldMappingsAsync) shares MapRuleEntityToDto — the additive fields must not break its existing deserialization/behavior (spec FR-16).</background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file>tests/unit/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests/</file>
      <file>src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/FieldMappings/FieldMappingEndpoints.cs</file>
    </relevant-files>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="ADR-038">Follow the KEEP-path test categories; do NOT add Mock&lt;HttpMessageHandler&gt;, DI-registration, or ctor null-check tests.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Publish-size ceiling ≤60 MB compressed; report absolute size + delta vs baseline (~49.63 MB incl. PDBs). Expected delta ≈ 0 (DTO fields only).</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Do NOT modify the push endpoint's behavior — this task only proves it still works.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <files>
      <file>.claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md</file>
      <file>.claude/constraints/testing.md</file>
      <file>docs/adr/ADR-038-testing-strategy.md</file>
      <file>.claude/constraints/azure-deployment.md</file>
    </files>
  </knowledge>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="1">Add/extend a test asserting MapRuleEntityToDto (or the endpoint response) populates mappingType/defaultValue/expression/isRequired/compatibilityMode from a representative rule entity.</step>
    <step order="2">Add/confirm a test that the push path (PushFieldMappingsAsync) still produces correct results with rules carrying the new fields (no deserialization break).</step>
    <step order="3">dotnet test the Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests project — all green.</step>
    <step order="4">Run: dotnet publish -c Release src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/ -o deploy/api-publish/ ; measure compressed size; record absolute + delta in notes.</step>
    <step order="5">Run dotnet list package --vulnerable --include-transitive ; confirm no new HIGH CVE; record in notes.</step>
    <step order="6">Update TASK-INDEX.md: mark 003 ✅.</step>
  </steps>

  <tools>
    <tool name="dotnet">Build, test, publish, list packages</tool>
  </tools>

  <outputs>
    <output type="test">tests/unit/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests/ (new/updated field-mapping DTO tests)</output>
    <output type="docs">projects/set-regarding-and-field-mapping-resolver-r2/notes/ (publish-size + CVE report)</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">A test asserts all five new rule-DTO fields project correctly.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">A test proves the push path works with the extended rule shape.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">dotnet test passes.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Publish size reported with delta vs baseline; ≤60 MB; notes updated.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">No new HIGH-severity CVE introduced.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>
    Ref: spec.md FR-16, NFR-01, NFR-07.

    Completed 2026-07-09. Added tests/unit/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests/Api/FieldMappings/FieldMappingRuleProjectionTests.cs
    (15 tests) covering MapRuleEntityToDto projection of the 5 new rule-DTO fields (all 4 MappingType
    branches + unknown-int fallback, DefaultValue/Expression/IsRequired passthrough, both CompatibilityMode
    branches + unknown-int fallback) and 2 push-path regression tests proving ApplyMappingRule still maps
    source-to-target correctly (Mapped + Skipped cases) when the rule carries the new fields.

    Code-review found MapRuleEntityToDto/ApplyMappingRule were private static, forcing a reflection seam
    (existing precedent: ChatEndpointsAttachmentsTests.cs). Found a cleaner seam: Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests already
    has InternalsVisibleTo, so both methods were changed private -> internal static (accessibility-only,
    zero behavior change) in FieldMappingEndpoints.cs, and the test calls them directly — no reflection,
    fully B8-compliant per tests/CLAUDE.md.

    dotnet test tests/unit/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests: 7662 passed, 0 failed, 101 skipped (pre-existing skips),
    Total 7763 — confirmed on 2 consecutive full runs after the accessibility change (one transient
    single-test flake in an intermediate run self-resolved on re-run; unrelated to this task's files).

    Publish size (dotnet publish -c Release, compressed via Compress-Archive -CompressionLevel Optimal):
    49.60 MB incl. PDBs (baseline ~49.63 MB, delta ~-0.03 MB) / 45.73 MB excl. PDBs (baseline 45.87 MB,
    delta ~-0.14 MB) -- both essentially flat vs baseline as expected (DTO fields + accessibility change
    only, no new packages). Well under the 60 MB ceiling.

    CVE scan (dotnet list package --vulnerable --include-transitive on Sprk.Bff.Api): 1 HIGH-severity
    finding, Microsoft.Kiota.Abstractions 1.21.2 (transitive via Microsoft.Graph). Confirmed PRE-EXISTING:
    `git diff origin/master...HEAD --stat -- '**/*.csproj'` is empty for this branch -- no package
    references were touched by tasks 001/002/003. Not a new CVE introduced by this task.

    Quality gates: code-review (1 finding -- B8 reflection seam -- remediated per above) and adr-check
    (0 violations; 1 pre-existing Warning noted -- test file lives at tests/unit/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests/Api/FieldMappings/,
    matching 100% of sibling FieldMapping tests in this project, which predates the tests/CLAUDE.md six-KEEP-path
    reorg referenced as "after task 050 path reorganization completes"; out of scope for this task to relocate
    the whole legacy test tree) both re-run clean after the fix.

    See notes/task-003-notes.md for the full report.
  </notes>

